From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: media: i2c: ov8856: add a keep_power bring-up parameter

When the probe fails (no ACK from the sensor) the driver powers the rails down
again, which makes it impossible to scan the CCI bus while the sensor is
actually powered.  keep_power=1 leaves the regulators and the MCLK on so the
bus can be probed with a user-space i2c scanner.

Bring-up aid only, not intended for merging.

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov8856.c	2026-11-07 22:02:12.416102182 +0800
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov8856.c	2026-11-07 22:02:12.420149257 +0800
@@ -103,6 +103,12 @@
 
 #define to_ov8856(_sd)			container_of(_sd, struct ov8856, sd)
 
+/* bring-up aid: keep the sensor powered after a failed probe so the CCI bus can
+ * be scanned while the rails and MCLK are actually on */
+static bool keep_power;
+module_param(keep_power, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(keep_power, "keep the sensor powered after a failed probe");
+
 static const char * const ov8856_supply_names[] = {
 	"dovdd",	/* Digital I/O power */
 	"avdd",		/* Analog power */
@@ -2453,7 +2459,10 @@
 	mutex_destroy(&ov8856->mutex);
 
 probe_power_off:
-	ov8856_power_off(ov8856->dev);
+	if (!keep_power)
+		ov8856_power_off(ov8856->dev);
+	else
+		dev_info(ov8856->dev, "keep_power: leaving the sensor powered for CCI scans\n");
 
 	return ret;
 }
